---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CANON_PATHS, LINKS, linkClass } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const ext = { target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" };

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is this a product review?",
    a: "No. It is doctrine — how to read the field. Definitions and the two intelligence models live on GunSearchEngine. The three-number desk is FFLIntel.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the fog of sell-through?",
    a: "Treating last month’s closed units as if they were the map of what people are trying to find now. A register series is an after-action report. The scout is the ask.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where should I go next?",
    a: "Fortress for the models. Demand Intelligence if you buy demand. GunSearchAgent if you run a site. FFLIntel issue 01 if you need the three numbers kept apart.",
  },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Fog of Sell-Through — Art of Demand | Betsy Tzu"
  description="Know the terrain before the register rings. Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. Betsy Tzu on the fog of closed units and the scout of shopper ask."
  path="/art-of-demand-retailbi"
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.tzu}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <p
      class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3"
    >
      Betsy Tzu · Art of Demand
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">
      Know the terrain before the register rings
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400 mb-6">
      Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. The wise operator still
      reads it — and does not march as if the river has not moved.
    </p>
    <figure class="mb-8">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.tzu)}
        alt="Betsy Tzu — The Art of Demand"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover ring-1 ring-zinc-700/80"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-zinc-600">
        Betsy Tzu — preparation over theater
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <blockquote
      class="mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-sky-500/25 bg-sky-950/20 px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 italic"
    >
      RetailBI’s intelligence is a byproduct of retail operations software.
      Betsy’s intelligence is a byproduct of product discovery.
      <footer class="mt-2 text-xs not-italic text-zinc-500">
        — frozen doctrine · Coriolis
      </footer>
    </blockquote>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
      <p>
        Classical strategy is obsessed with the map you hold when you still have
        a choice. In 2A retail the choice is the order, the floor set, the page
        you merchandize before Saturday. Closed units from a prior window are
        true. They are also late. They tell you where the army already camped —
        not where the next column is walking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Call that delay the <strong class="text-zinc-200">fog of sell-through</strong
        >. A register series is an after-action report: same-store new units,
        a monthly print, a honest count of what rang. Useful. Incomplete. The
        scout is the ask — the caliber, the load, the model someone typed when
        nothing on the shelf answered back. Zero-hit demand never becomes a
        unit. It still happened.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three numbers keep getting folded into one headline. Background checks
        are weather: public, lagged, not sales. The Index is the after-action:
        what a reporting panel actually sold. The ask is the terrain underfoot
        — including ground nobody rang up. Collapse them and you plan from a
        myth. Keep them apart and you can still use each one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Supreme excellence is not shouting at last month’s percent-change. It is
        knowing the field while the shopper is still hunting. The dealer who
        reads the ask on their own site is not guessing the next case. The brand
        that buys anonymized search intent is not waiting for a closed period to
        learn the river moved. Doctrine without a sensor is theater. The sensor
        on the dealer site is{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a>. The
        OEM door is{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.demandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Demand Intelligence</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page is culture, not a definition dump and not a comparison grid.
        The models live at the fortress. The desk that refuses to let three
        numbers become one is FFLIntel. Walk there when you want the field
        report — not a poem.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href={LINKS.fortress}
        {...ext}
        class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-5 hover:border-sky-500/40"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Fortress · the models</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-500">
          Sell-through vs search intent — GunSearchEngine
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href={LINKS.demandIntel}
        {...ext}
        class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-5 hover:border-sky-500/40"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Enterprise</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-500">Demand Intelligence for OEMs</p>
      </a>
      <a
        href={LINKS.gsa}
        {...ext}
        class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-5 hover:border-sky-500/40"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">GunSearchAgent</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-500">
          Free demand sensor on the dealer site
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href={LINKS.fflintelIssue01}
        {...ext}
        class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-5 hover:border-sky-500/40"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">FFLIntel · issue 01</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-500">
          Three numbers. Do not make them one.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-4">Short FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="space-y-5">
        {
          faqs.map((item) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-100">{item.q}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">{item.a}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
      Not affiliated with Gearfire or RetailBI. Marks belong to their owners.
      Not 4473 / ATF software. Not a POS. Not a NICS system. Culture essay —
      ranking definitions stay on{" "}
      <a href={LINKS.fortress} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline" {...ext}
        >gunsearchengine.com/betsy-vs-retailbi</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
